\ A synthetic frame queued while a compiled body unwinds a recovered error must not resurface
\ as the innermost frame of the next, unrelated error.
\
\ The eager suite reuses this golden, so passing both modes is the parity check. The recovered
\ error's `#each` unwind queues a frame after capture already ran; the `+` raise below must
\ render its own frame, not the leftover.
mid: ( -- ) [ 1 0 / drop ] ;
outer: ( -- ) [ { 1 } [ drop mid ] #each ] ;
[ outer ] [ drop ] recover
"z" 1 +
